# Selective Multiscale Arithmetic Positivity

Umbrella for selective positivity of the Weil form on complete, self-similar arithmetic sources:
selection of `Λ` by atomic positivity at every root, the pole hyperplane as the harmonic hyperplane,
the full-form separation of `ζ` from its Liouville twin there, the conductor-two excitation and the
two-sided selective margin, the twin-blindness of the high-detail Haar floor, the renormalization
calculus of a refinement level, and the dyadic multiresolution of the complete source with its
level-Toeplitz law. See `SelectiveMultiscaleArithmeticPositivity/README.md`.
